## Principles

- **The app reads a contract, not the tables.** The browser app reads only the versioned `v_*` views
  (docs/contract.md), from an in-memory snapshot that holds nothing else. The ingestion can change its tables
  freely. `tests/app/test_contract_only.py` enforces the split.
- **Nothing personal goes into git.** Settings, secrets and data stay in gitignored files.
- **The database may be the only copy.** No code drops a table; schema changes are migrations.

## Components

| Part | Code | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Ingestion | `src/{{ package }}/ingest/` | reads the sources, merges into the tables |
| Storage | `src/{{ package }}/db/` | `schema.sql` (tables, then the contract views), `store.py` (version, migrations) |
| Contract | `src/{{ package }}/contract/` | `schema.sql` (the reference schema), the rules |
| Browser app | `src/{{ package }}/app/`, `query/` | pages in `app/views/`; queries on the views only |
| Shared code | `duckkit` | from the scaffold: snapshots, publish, backups, serving, the standard commands |

